  "Limits": "Private cache checks compare every run against independently sampled pixels. Instrumented cache counts use two existing negatives, two PDF417-only passes with a 60,000 ms diagnostic allowance to complete all work; their timings are unranked. The actual baseline/current cache source is retained in the archive. Cache byte accounting is an estimate and excludes other decoder working memory; no peak-memory claim is made. The paired controls and whole-image costs preserve the 1,500 ms allowance, preloaded pixels, hints and empty oracles. Shared-host load limits portable latency and completion claims.",
